ggml patches for llama.cpp v0.5.0 (ggml 0.25.1), used by julia1-cli (https://github.com/alucassch/julia1-cli).
Paths are relative to the llama.cpp root: `patch -p1` (or `git apply`) there, or `patch -p2` inside a copy of its ggml/.
CMakeLists.txt applies it to a copy of the fetched ggml/ in the build directory (JULIA1_GGML_PATCH=ON, the default).
SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
Copyright (c) 2026 the julia1-cli authors. MIT like ggml, so that the changes can go upstream (the rest of julia1-cli
is Apache-2.0); the license text is in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES, entry (1).

Changes (the comments in the code carry the same labels):
  P1   Metal: exact kernel_mul_mm variants that stage the operands as float (F32 weights) or half (F16 weights, lossless),
       selected by ggml_prec_set_src(mul_mat, GGML_PREC_F32, 1)
  P2   Metal: exact flash attention that stages Q as float (non-vec kernel, F32 K/V, dk = dv = 64), selected by
       ggml_prec_set_acc(flash_attn_ext, GGML_PREC_F32)
  P3   CPU (aarch64 NEON): vectorised GEGLU with erf
  P4   CPU: flash attention chunked by whole Q tiles
  P6   Metal: residual ADD fused into the kernel_mul_mm epilogue
  P7   Metal: GEGLU fused into the kernel_mul_mm epilogue
  P8   Metal: bias, ReLU and residual fused into the kernel_mul_mm epilogue
  P9   Metal: NEOX RoPE fused into the kernel_mul_mm epilogue
  P10  Metal: kernel_mul_mm_t, smaller GEMM tiles for small grids
  P11  Metal: flash attention with n_kv % 64 != 0 (K/V padding copies only the row payload; a fully masked partial last
       KV block is skipped)
  P12  CPU (Apple): large F32 matmuls through Accelerate inside the CPU backend
ggml.h defines GGML_JULIA1_EXACT_MM (P1, P2), GGML_JULIA1_FA_KVPAD (P11) and, on Apple, GGML_JULIA1_CPU_ACCELERATE (P12).

diff -ru a/ggml/include/ggml.h b/ggml/include/ggml.h
--- a/ggml/include/ggml.h
+++ b/ggml/include/ggml.h
@@ -1476,6 +1476,18 @@
             enum ggml_prec       prec,
             int                  idx);
 
+    // julia1 patch P1, P2: the Metal backend honours ggml_prec_set_src(mul_mat, GGML_PREC_F32, 1) and
+    // ggml_prec_set_acc(flash_attn_ext, GGML_PREC_F32) with float-staged kernel variants
+#define GGML_JULIA1_EXACT_MM 1
+    // julia1 patch P11: Metal flash attention with n_kv % 64 != 0 costs about what the next multiple of 64 does (the
+    // kvpad pre-pass copies only the rows' payload; a partial last KV block is skipped when fully masked)
+#define GGML_JULIA1_FA_KVPAD 1
+    // julia1 patch P12: on Apple the CPU backend (built with GGML_ACCELERATE, ggml's default there) runs large F32 x F32
+    // matmuls through Accelerate itself, as the BLAS backend would
+#if defined(__APPLE__)
+#define GGML_JULIA1_CPU_ACCELERATE 1
+#endif
